      "lineNbr": 510,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-27T21:33:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a reason the rounding-to-sizeofT behavior doesn\u0027t live in SkContainerAllocator? I was surprised to see it still here, after seeing that the SkContainerAllocator already knows `sizeOfT` and the allocator has methods with names like `roundUpCapacity`. (We might even be able to avoid the divide if we structure it right?)\n\nAfter reading through the rest of this CL, this is my biggest question. The rest of the comments are all nits but this seems like an important function for the the ContainerAllocator to actually take responsibility for, esp. since it seems to have all the moving pieces necessary to centralize the logic.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 506,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 510,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "51833ff0e4d0b72c0f4c4bd2288e86b154893fd6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "468782a2_8a1dbc4a",
        "filename": "include/private/SkTArray.h",
        "patchSetId": 26
      },
      "lineNbr": 510,
      "author": {
        "id": 5210
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-28T14:41:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is on purpose. The divide done by SkContainerAllocator would need to use the idiv instruction which on skylake takes 42-95 cycles according to agner.org. Since, the divide is done here the size is know at compile time, and likely strength reduced to a shift with a latency of 1. I had problems with this in some of my original SkTDArray work. I sympathise with your observation, but I think this is a good optimization, and not too onerous. I will add a comment explaining this.",
      "parentUuid": "0f720c42_d8431b0c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 506,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 510,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "51833ff0e4d0b72c0f4c4bd2288e86b154893fd6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a9eb1756_042ad665",
        "filename": "include/private/SkTArray.h",
        "patchSetId": 26
